{
  "name": "Webhook: create a Social Poster post from a shop or form request",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "8c6bda7c-8d64-42ae-8969-8877f47a32c6",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -320,
        -60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### How it works\nThis workflow accepts an HTTP POST from a shop, a form or another app and turns it into a Social Poster post. It first checks that a caption is present in `caption`, `text` or `message`. If the text is missing, it responds with status 400 and creates no post. If the text is present, it maps the link, title and publicly reachable media URLs from the request. “Settings and fields” holds the account reference and lead time. When scheduling is requested (`schedule` true or omitted), Social Poster creates the draft, schedules it at least five minutes in the future, and confirms publishing. If you set `schedule` to false, it only creates a draft for review. The response includes the draft id. Nothing is published immediately.\n\n### Setup\nThis template uses the unverified community node `n8n-nodes-social-poster` (tested with version 0.1.1). It runs on self-hosted n8n only, not on n8n Cloud. Install it under Settings → Community Nodes → Install, package name `n8n-nodes-social-poster`. Guide: https://docs.n8n.io/integrations/community-nodes/installation/\nCreate a “Social Poster API” credential (key under the account menu → AI access → API key for n8n, base URL `https://app.social-poster.io`).\nIn “Settings and fields”, enter the account reference (`acc_…`) and the minutes (at least 5). Select the credential on both Social Poster nodes. Save the workflow, copy the production webhook URL and send JSON such as `{\"caption\":\"Test post\",\"link\":\"https://example.com\",\"schedule\":false}`. Check the draft in Social Poster before you connect a live system. If n8n is reachable from the internet, protect the webhook, for example with header auth. Never send the API key in the webhook request.\n\n### Customization\nYou can rename the payload fields to match your form, or always create drafts only. Leave “X Content Reviewed” off until a person has checked the exact text for X (Twitter).",
        "height": 1040,
        "width": 680,
        "color": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "93aec3be-30c8-410d-bfec-d4e61c454629",
      "name": "Receive the request",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        460,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Webhook and checks\nOnly requests with a caption continue. Requests without text receive status 400.",
        "height": 240,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "032c0a12-cb23-4bdc-ac71-32f091691d4b",
